This game was the last of the trilogy I've finished and I was afraid of not ejoying it because of it being old. Not even close to that, this game doesn't look old or dated. It actually SUMS up to the other games in gameplay, story and graphics. As with the other games, the immersion in this one is exceptional and gameplay and controls are tight. If you are in doubt about getting this game after finishing the newer ones, this is a no brainer.
To the people who never played this game, you're missing a lot by skipping this one.
I'll list some stuff I have liked about this game over the others:
- It kinda do a bit of platforming, I was really impressed because I didn't experience a good jump and miss platform in a 3D game;
- The story is so great, Joker is at his best and you can feel how evil he is (I'm pretty sure this will make me play the other games again looking at him like the real bad guy;
- Boss fights are the best. Bosses encounters are a special moment where you'll enjoy the challenge while not getting punished too much;
- The villains, oh my... They have so much depth and you really get  afraid of their power;
- The way Joker is always playing with Batman is genial.
It took me 12 hours to finish the game (66% of progress).
10/10 easy
